
🗓️ Day 2 | 21 Days SQL Challenge with Indian Data Club 💚

📍 Topic: Using the WHERE Clause to Filter Data

💬 Today’s Focus:
Today’s challenge was all about filtering data — learning to pull out only the rows that truly matter. It felt like solving a mini mystery 🕵️‍♂️, searching through data to uncover the exact information I needed!

🧩 Challenge:
Retrieve all patients who were admitted under the ‘Surgery’ department and have a satisfaction score below 70. Display their patient_id, name, age, and satisfaction score.

💻 My Query:

SELECT patient_id, name, age, satisfaction 
FROM patients 
WHERE service = 'Surgery' 
AND satisfaction < 70;


🚀 What I Learned:
The WHERE clause is a powerful tool in SQL — it acts like a filter that helps focus on relevant data. I also explored how logical operators like AND and OR make queries more flexible and precise.

🎯 Key Takeaway:
Smart filtering brings meaningful insights to the surface 📊
Each SQL query sharpens my analytical mindset — one challenge at a time!

